SUMMARY:May Free First Sunday
DESCRIPTION:Join the Japanese American Museum of Oregon for April Free First Sunday! \n\n\n\nMay Free First Sunday is generously sponsored by Anne Naito-Campbell & Oregon Rises Above Hate. \n\n\n\nAdmission is free all day\, 11am-4pm. \n\n\n\nCelebrate Children’s Day! Come fold origami samurai helmets\, a Kodomo no hi (Children’s Day) tradition and view our exhibition Minidoka on Our Minds. \n\n\n\nAll ages are welcome.
URL:https://jamo.org/event/may-free-first-sunday/
LOCATION:Japanese American Museum of Oregon\, 411 NW Flanders Street (Entrance on NW 4th Ave)\, Portland\, OR\, 97209
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jamo.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-Free-First-Sunday-Insta-45.jpg
END:VEVENT
